 "short_name": "Alfred Duma",
 "_doc": "TAX INVOICE/STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT, emunsoft ledger family (same engine as KwaDukuza / Abaqulusi / Bela-Bela). Masthead 'ALFRED DUMA LOCAL MUNICIPALITY / PO BOX 29 LADYSMITH, KZN 3370', VAT No.:4450274669. Fingerprint = masthead AND that VAT number, so it can never match a sibling emunsoft municipality. LAYOUT: header block of 'Label: value' pairs (Account Number / Account Date / Consumer Name / Tax Invoice No. / ERF Description / Suburb / Street / Market Value / Land Area / Deposit / Internet PIN). Then 'METER READINGS' with columns METER NO. / METER TYPE / OLD READING / NEW READING / CONSUMPTION / LEVIED AMOUNT / READING DATES -- note this municipality prints CONSUMPTION *before* LEVIED AMOUNT and has NO 'READING TYPE' column (Bela-Bela's variant of the same engine puts READING DATE + READING TYPE before CONSUMPTION and prints no LEVIED AMOUNT). READING DATES is a range 'dd/mm/yyyy - dd/mm/yyyy'; on one bill the range start is blank and the cell reads '- 17/02/2026', and on one bill the LEVIED AMOUNT cell is empty for every meter. Then 'ACCOUNT DETAILS' ledger DATE / CODE / DESCRIPTION / UNITS / TARIFF / VALUE. Codes seen across the 10-bill set: 007030 electricity, 008888 payment, 009008 VAT. This account is ELECTRICITY ONLY -- no water/sewer/refuse/rates lines exist, so those services are correctly absent. Electricity ledger shapes: 'ELECTRICITY CONS' (kWh @ 4.0742 -- the energy line), 'ELECTRICITY CONS BASIC CHARGE' (1.000 @ 212.29 -- note it starts with the same words, so the energy pattern uses a negative lookahead for ' BASIC'), 'FINAL USAGE ELECTRICIY' (sic, misspelt on the bill -- negative kWh reversals at the same tariff when a meter is closed off), 'RAISING OF ELECT CONS-06/25 TO 04/26' (a prior-period correction, .000 units, R129,685.20 on one bill) and 'TRF BILLING FROM A/C [number removed] TO [number removed] <date>' transfer lines that print the date and code AFTER the description and end in '(TRANSFER)'. SUMMING CHOICES: standard_kwh / standard_r = ELECTRICITY CONS + FINAL USAGE ELECTRICIY netted together (both are metered consumption at the same 4.0742 tariff, the second simply negative) -- the netted pair keeps R/kWh == 4.0742 exactly. other_r = BASIC CHARGE + RAISING OF ELECT CONS + TRANSFERS: those three carry no kWh (units .000) so folding them into the energy band would break the kWh<->Rand ratio. total_kwh is taken from the METER READINGS CONSUMPTION column (summed) so it stays INDEPENDENT of the ledger kWh in standard_kwh -- the two agree on all 10 bills, which is the real self-check. Single band only: this is a flat-rate LV supply, no TOU, no demand, no NMD, no reading-type column -> those canonical columns are '_none'. RULE ZERO: the bill prints NO independent ex-VAT current-charges total (the ageing row's CURRENT column is a balance, not a levy), so total_ex_vat_r IS the sum of the parts and the reconcile leg is structurally circular -- see the report. The genuine checks are (a) sum(METER READINGS LEVIED AMOUNT) == standard_r, (b) sum(METER READINGS CONSUMPTION) == standard_kwh, (c) printed VAT == 15% of total_ex_vat_r.",
